{
  "id": "COMPOUND:279 - DISEASE:293",
  "verbalization": "Atomoxetine exerts a direct influence on synaptotagmin 17, a protein involved in synaptic vesicle trafficking, which in turn contributes to the development of Atrioventricular block NOS. This relationship is supported by multiple high-scoring pathways, all of which establish a causal link between atomoxetine and the condition through synaptotagmin 17. The consistent evidence across these paths suggests that synaptotagmin 17 acts as a critical mediator in the pathophysiology of Atrioventricular block NOS, likely by modulating cardiac electrical conduction. The mechanism is further supported by the observed scores, which indicate a strong and reliable association between atomoxetine and the condition. While the exact molecular pathways remain partially unknown, the integrated evidence points to synaptotagmin 17 as a central node in the regulatory network linking atomoxetine to Atrioventricular block NOS.",
